  "raw": "en Español\n\n219 \nABNT20 KNHC 291738\nTWOAT \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 PM EDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nFor the North Atlantic...Caribbean Sea and the Gulf of America:\n\nEast of the Leeward Islands (Remnants of Dolly):\nDisorganized showers and thunderstorm continue in association with \nthe remnants of Tropical Storm Dolly, located about 300 miles east \nof the Leeward Islands. However, there are no signs that the system \nis developing a closed circulation. Redevelopment of this system is \nunlikely while it moves westward to west-northwestward near 25 mph. \nThe wave could bring locally heavy rains and gusty winds to \nportions of the Leeward Islands, the Virgin Islands and Puerto Rico \nover the next several days.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...10 percent.\n\nNortheastern and North-Central Gulf of America:\nCloudiness and showers associated with a weak low pressure area \ncentered about 125 miles south of Pensacola, Florida, have become a \nlittle better organized since yesterday.  Some additional slow \ndevelopment of this system is possible during the next few days as \nit drifts westward.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...20 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Beven"
